  "note": "Re-judged 2026-10-24 (independent auditor, after 8a340e018a). RFC 8654 Section 3: \"Peers that wish to use the BGP Extended Message Capability MUST support error handling for BGP UPDATE messages per [RFC7606].\" The only changed unit is TestRFC7606MPReachNLRIConsistentWithAFISAFIAccepted: its doc comment dropped the stale word \"Untagged\" (the finding the previous re-judgement recorded); body unchanged, an IPv4 MP_REACH whose /8 ends flush with the attribute gives exact ActionNone through ValidateUpdateRFC7606, ran green. That message-level positive (and its sibling negative TestRFC7606AttributeLengthConflictTreatAsWithdraw) proves only the RFC 7606 classifier and carries no Extended Message context; the requirement's proof rests on the unchanged session-level pairs in rfc_receive_session_dispatch_test.go and rfc8654_rib_recovery_test.go, which on a session that negotiated Extended Message and with UPDATEs over 4096 octets assert the exact RFC 7606 outcomes (attribute discard, duplicate removal, duplicate-MP 3/1 reset, treat-as-withdraw removing installed routes from Adj-RIB-In and Loc-RIB) with conforming positives. Verdict stands.",
